Condition : 3 - Prior to the installation of the air source heat pump, details of the acoustic enclosure to be provided around the unit shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The submitted details shall include:
a) scaled drawings and specifications of the enclosure;
b) details of the materials and acoustic performance of the enclosure;
c) calculations demonstrating that the enclosure will achieve the noise mitigation measures and noise limits recommended within the approved KP Acoustics Planning Compliance Report reference 27330.PCR.01.RevB dated 17 April 2026

The air source heat pump shall not be used until the approved acoustic enclosure has been installed in accordance with the approved details and shall thereafter be permanently retained and maintained as approved.
Reason: In the interests of neighbouring amenity in accordance with Council policy LP2 of the Local Plan
